-- APPENDIX A: FUTURE/TARGET SCHEMA (v5–v8)
-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
--
-- The tables below were defined in schema_updates_v5 through v8. They represent
-- the target multi-tenant, central identity, and transportation architecture.
--
-- ⚠️  THESE MAY OR MAY NOT EXIST IN THE LIVE DATABASE.
-- Since Spec 01 skipped live introspection, their deployment status is unknown.
-- Verify before building features that depend on them.
--
-- They are NOT used by any current application code (the app runs on the
-- legacy tables above). Spec 02 will migrate profiles → persons/employees/students.
--
-- Source files (now in database/migrations/):
--   v5: schema_updates_v5_foundation.sql — organizations, institutions, RBAC,
--       persons, employees, teachers, drivers, students (new model)
--   v6: schema_updates_v6_students.sql — academic_years, classes, sections,
--       admissions, student_enrollments, student_documents
--   v7: schema_updates_v7_academic.sql — departments, courses, subjects,
--       teacher_assignments
--   v8: schema_updates_v8_transportation.sql — vehicles, routes, route_stops,
--       driver_assignments, student_transport_assignments, transport_fees,
--       gps_locations
--
-- Note: v5 redefines `students` with a person_id FK — this conflicts with the
-- legacy flat `students` table in Section 6. The legacy table is what the app
-- uses today. The v5 version is the Spec 02 migration target.
--
-- RLS is enabled on all v5–v8 tables, but most have NO policies defined yet
-- (only v7 has admin + authenticated-read policies). Policies must be added
-- before any of these tables can be used with the anon/authenticated key.
-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
